From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0165] sweet gpu: GPU timestamps of each submission (gpu_ts=1)


"The GPU worked N us" is ring write to the first poll that sees the fence: it
includes queueing behind earlier submissions and the poll delay, so it cannot
say whether the GPU is saturated or what one submission costs on the GPU.

With gpu_ts=1 every submission gets CP_REG_TO_MEM of CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER
(0x980, Linux a6xx get_stats_counter) before its IBs and CP_EVENT_WRITE
RB_DONE_TS|TIMESTAMP (mesa fd6_record_ts) after them, into a 16-byte slot at
+0x100 of the fence page (64 slots, inside the 4 KiB already mapped at GPU VA
0x10020000). Every five seconds: "RedwoodGPU: GPU timestamps (0165): busy B us
of S us (P %), exec E us mean over N submissions, counter T ticks in U us",
where busy excludes the time a submission queued behind the previous one and
the last pair gives the counter's real rate. Off by default: the ring words
are unchanged without the boot-arg.
---
